{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"requirements analysis requirements analysis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md","fileName":"Requirements Analysis.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Requirements Analysis","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[UX Evaluation]] [[Software Engineering]] [[Software Requirements Elicitation and Specification]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["UX Evaluation","Software Engineering","Software Requirements Elicitation and Specification","User-Centered Design","Task Analysis","Prototype","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"requirements analysis requirements analysis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md","fileName":"Requirements Analysis.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Requirements Analysis","heading":"Requirements Analysis","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Requirements analysis investigates intended users, their activities, and their environment before a new design is built. Here, work includes employment, learning, play, or any activity the system is meant to support.\n\nContextual inquiry gathers evidence through observation, interviews, recordings, and existing work artifacts. Contextual analysis organizes and interprets that evidence into models of users, tasks, relationships, artifacts, and physical settings. Requirements are then extracted from the problems and opportunities found.\n\nThis work grounds [[User-Centered Design]] in actual context and supplies inputs to [[Task Analysis]], design, and [[Prototype|prototyping]].\n\nArchitectural analysis also classifies statements into behavior and quality constraints, resolves conflicts, and tests feasibility against schedule, budget, technology, and the expected operating environment.","tags":["baby"],"links":["UX Evaluation","Software Engineering","Software Requirements Elicitation and Specification","User-Centered Design","Task Analysis","Prototype","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"requirements analysis requirements analysis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Requirements Analysis.md","fileName":"Requirements Analysis.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Requirements Analysis","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["UX Evaluation","Software Engineering","Software Requirements Elicitation and Specification","User-Centered Design","Task Analysis","Prototype","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}